{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '150,205p'; git diff -- test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc | tail -115; rg -n '349525|349,525|349000|3000|nanoTime|elapsed|deadline|linear' test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc; tail -35 collab/1791284684337-repl-engineer-head-h3-followups-r2.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\"","aggregated_output":"   150\t  [records]\n   151\t  (str (pr-str records) \"\\n\"))\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn- without-boms\n   155\t  \"`text` without its leading byte order marks, every one of them: one\n   156\t   policy on every host, whose decoders differ (Node's drops one, the\n   157\t   JVM's keeps U+FEFF).  The run is scanned by index and cut once, so a\n   158\t   file of marks costs one pass, not one copy per mark.\"\n   159\t  [text]\n   160\t  (let [n (count text)\n   161\t        i (loop [i 0]\n   162\t            (if (and (< i n) (= \"\\uFEFF\" (subs text i (inc i))))\n   163\t              (recur (inc i))\n   164\t              i))]\n   165\t    (if (zero? i) text (subs text i))))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t(defn read-heads\n   169\t  \"The persisted head records of the store directory `dir`: `{:records\n   170\t   r}`, an empty version-1 record when no `heads.edn` exists, or\n   171\t   `{:refusal text}`: a file that cannot be read, holds more than\n   172\t   `heads-max-bytes`, is not valid UTF-8, holds a byte order mark\n   173\t   anywhere but at its start, or is not exactly one version-1 record.\n   174\t   Never throws.\"\n   175\t  [dir]\n   176\t  (let [path (str dir \"/\" heads-file)\n   177\t        bs (try (fs/read-bounded path heads-max-bytes)\n   178\t                (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   179\t                  {::failed (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))\n   180\t        text (when (and (some? bs) (not (map? bs))\n   181\t                        (<= (fs/byte-length bs) heads-max-bytes))\n   182\t               (try (fs/decode-utf8 bs)\n   183\t                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   184\t                      ::invalid)))\n   185\t        body (when (string? text) (without-boms text))]\n   186\t    (cond\n   187\t      (nil? bs) {:records {:version 1 :heads {}}}\n   188\t      (map? bs) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it cannot be read (\"\n   189\t                               (::failed bs) \")\")}\n   190\t      (nil? text) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it holds more than \"\n   191\t                                 heads-max-bytes \" bytes\")}\n   192\t      (= ::invalid text) {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path\n   193\t                                        \": it is not valid UTF-8\")}\n   194\t      ;; a mark past the leading run is refused before the reader sees\n   195\t      ;; it: one host's reader takes it for whitespace, another's for a\n   196\t      ;; token, and a record never holds one\n   197\t      (str/includes? body \"\\uFEFF\")\n   198\t      {:refusal (str \"heads file \" path \": it is not valid: a byte order \"\n   199\t                     \"mark (U+FEFF) follows its start\")}\n   200\t\n   201\t      :else (parse-heads path body))))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t;; =============================================================================\n   205\t;; The board and the deposit (5.4)\n+      (is (= [(str \"dht: the head trace of \" m2 \" was not deposited: \"\n+                   \":yin.head/seq-regression\")]\n+             refused)\n+          (pr-str (get-in w [:lines :a]))))\n+    (testing \"the HEAD write did not fail\"\n+      (is (= \"{:type :closure}\" answer) \"the evaluation answered\")\n+      (is (str/includes? (str (fs/read-file-text dir \"HEAD\")) (str m2)))\n+      (is (= forged (get-in (board-trace w) [:yin.head/envelope\n+                                             :yin.head/manifest]))\n+          \"a refusal appends nothing\"))\n+    (testing \"a later deposit, once the board admits it, is made\"\n+      (stream/append! board t1)\n+      (let [w (run (publish! w 3) 20 (fn [_] false))\n+            m3 (get-in w [:a :repl :indexer :manifest-address])]\n+        (is (not= m2 m3))\n+        (is (= m3 (get-in (board-trace w) [:yin.head/envelope\n+                                           :yin.head/manifest])))\n+        (is (= 1 (count (lines-with w :a \"was not deposited\")))\n+            \"nothing more is reported\")\n+        (close! w)))))\n+\n+\n ;; =============================================================================\n ;; The moved line names only new moves; a dial failure prints once\n ;; =============================================================================\n \n+(def ^:private second-pub-port 13)\n+\n+\n+(defn- moved-by-installs\n+  \"A reader of two publishers, A (`key`, alib from `a-code`) and C\n+   (`other`, the module `c-name` from `c-code`), that linked both names;\n+   then both republish (`a-code'`, `c-code'`) and the reader installs\n+   both heads.  Answers the moved lines `moved-lines` derives for those\n+   two installs taken as one step: the reader's node before them, its\n+   node after, and both `:installed` events.\"\n+  [key other c-name [a-code a-code'] [c-code c-code']]\n+  (let [p1 (sign/principal (:public key))\n+        p2 (sign/principal (:public other))\n+        w (world)\n+        w (assoc w\n+                 :a (publisher w key (temp-dir))\n+                 :c (shell {:mesh (:mesh w) :ws (:ws w) :dir (temp-dir)\n+                            :port second-pub-port :peers [reader-port]\n+                            :key other :principals []})\n+                 :b (reader w key (temp-dir)\n+                            {:peers [pub-port second-pub-port]\n+                             :principals [(:public key) (:public other)]\n+                             :follow [{:principal (:public key)\n+                                       :host \"127.0.0.1\" :port pub-port}\n+                                      {:principal (:public other)\n+                                       :host \"127.0.0.1\"\n+                                       :port second-pub-port}]}))\n+        publish (fn [w k n code]\n+                  (-> w\n+                      (type! k (str \"(def f (fn [] \" code \"))\"))\n+                      (type! k \"(require (quote yin.link))\")\n+                      (type! k (str \"(yin.link/publish (quote \" n\n+                                    \") (quote [f]))\"))))\n+        newest #(get-in %1 [%2 :repl :indexer :manifest-address])\n+        caught-up #(and (= (newest % :a) (:manifest (heads-of % :b key)))\n+                        (= (newest % :c) (:manifest (heads-of % :b other))))\n+        w (-> w\n+              (publish :a \"alib\" a-code)\n+              (publish :c c-name c-code)\n+              (run 3000 caught-up)\n+              (type! :b \"(require (quote alib))\")\n+              (type! :b (str \"(require (quote \" c-name \"))\"))\n+              (run 3000 #(not (pending? % :b))))\n+        _ (is (= (symbol c-name) (value w :b)) (pr-str (get-in w [:lines :b])))\n+        before (get-in w [:b :repl :dht])\n+        w (-> w\n+              (publish :a \"alib\" a-code')\n+              (publish :c c-name c-code')\n+              (run 3000 caught-up))\n+        _ (is (caught-up w) (pr-str (get-in w [:lines :b])))\n+        installed [{:yin.head/event :installed :principal p1\n+                    :trace (:installed (heads-of w :b key))}\n+                   {:yin.head/event :installed :principal p2\n+                    :trace (:installed (heads-of w :b other))}]\n+        lines (repl.dht/moved-lines (get-in w [:b :repl]) before\n+                                    (get-in w [:b :repl :dht]) installed)]\n+    (close! w)\n+    lines))\n+\n+\n+(deftest the-moved-line-names-the-principal-that-moved-each-name\n+  (let [key (sign/generate)\n+        other (sign/generate)\n+        p1 (sign/principal (:public key))\n+        p2 (sign/principal (:public other))\n+        head-of (fn [line] (re-find #\"\\(head of [^)]*\\)\" (str line)))]\n+    (testing \"two principals installed in one step, each moving its own name\"\n+      (let [lines (moved-by-installs key other \"blib\" [1 2] [10 20])\n+            line-of (fn [n] (first (filter #(str/starts-with?\n+                                               % (str \"dht: \" n \" moved: \"))\n+                                           lines)))]\n+        (is (= 2 (count lines)) (pr-str lines))\n+        (is (str/includes? (str (head-of (line-of \"alib\"))) p1) (pr-str lines))\n+        (is (not (str/includes? (str (head-of (line-of \"alib\"))) p2))\n+            (pr-str lines))\n+        (is (str/includes? (str (head-of (line-of \"blib\"))) p2) (pr-str lines))\n+        (is (not (str/includes? (str (head-of (line-of \"blib\"))) p1))\n+            (pr-str lines))))\n+    (testing \"two principals installed in one step, moving the same name\n+              together: both are named\"\n+      (let [lines (moved-by-installs key other \"alib\" [1 2] [1 2])]\n+        (is (= 1 (count lines)) (pr-str lines))\n+        (is (str/includes? (str (head-of (first lines))) p1) (pr-str lines))\n+        (is (str/includes? (str (head-of (first lines))) p2)\n+            (pr-str lines))))))\n+\n (deftest a-move-is-reported-once-and-each-name-its-own\n   (let [key (sign/generate)\n         w (world)\n361:          w (run w 3000 #(and (not (pending? % :b)) ((installed? :b key) %)))\n383:              w (run w 3000 #(not= m1 (:manifest (heads-of % :b key))))\n403:                  w (run w 3000 #(not (pending? % :b)))\n424:                             (run 3000 #(not (pending? % :b)))\n469:        w (run w 3000 #(seq (lines-with % :b \":yin.head/unpersisted\")))]\n480:    (let [w (run w 3000 (installed? :b key))]\n522:        w (run (publish! w 1) 3000 (installed? :b key))\n530:            w (run w 3000 #(seq (lines-with % :b \":yin.head/unpersisted\")))\n546:            w (run w 3000 #(seq (lines-with % :b \"crashed before the rename\")))\n562:                w (run w 3000 #(= newest (:manifest (heads-of % :b key))))]\n574:            w (run w 3000 (fn [_] (= newest (written))))\n859:                [[\"only marks, up to the bound\" (marks 349525) false]\n860:                 [\"marks, then the record\" (into (marks 349000)\n871:              (is (< took 3000) (str label \": \" took \" ms\")))))))\n1017:              (run 3000 caught-up)\n1020:              (run 3000 #(not (pending? % :b))))\n1026:              (run 3000 caught-up))\n1076:        w (run w 3000 caught-up)\n1080:              (run 3000 #(not (pending? % :b))))\n1086:                (run 3000 caught-up))\n1088:          w (-> w (type! :a \"(def unrelated 3)\") (run 3000 caught-up))\n1094:                (run 3000 caught-up))]\n1208:     ;; test, and fails at the deadline.\nSession-ID: 3a4d543e-01d3-49d0-892d-61355cef093b\n\nBoth BOM findings are fixed and green on the JVM, Node and Dart, and the full `bb test:clj` passes. I only changed `src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc` and `test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc`. The fs helpers are untouched, so the fs test namespace didn't change.\n\n## 1. Quadratic copying: done\n**What changed:** `without-boms` now scans the leading run of U+FEFF by index, one one-character `subs` per position, and then cuts the string once with `(subs text i)`. If there is no leading mark, the text comes back unchanged. `read-heads` binds the stripped text once as `body`.\n\n**Test:** in `heads-edn-is-bounded-and-strict-utf-8`, the case \"a file of marks is scanned once, in bounded time\" uses explicit bytes:\n- A file of only marks, 349,525 of them (1,048,575 bytes, just under the bound), must be refused, and the record parser refuses the empty text that is left.\n- 349,000 marks followed by the record must read as the record.\n- Each case must finish in under 3000 ms.\n\n**Fails without the change:** with the round-1 code restored, the JVM took 9322 ms and 8058 ms, and both timing assertions failed.\n\n## 2. A BOM after the leading run: done\n**What changed:** after the leading marks are removed, any U+FEFF left anywhere in the text is refused before the EDN reader sees it, on every host. The refusal reads `heads file <path>: it is not valid: a byte order mark (U+FEFF) follows its start`. The `read-heads` docstring now lists this case. The other refusals and their order are unchanged.\n\n**Test:** \"a byte order mark past the leading run is refused…\" uses explicit bytes for four placements, each expecting that refusal:\n- between tokens;\n- just before a closer;\n- inside a string;\n- a leading mark plus the record plus a trailing mark.\n\nThe earlier leading-BOM cases (1, 2 and 3 marks) still read as the record.\n\n**Fails without the change:** with the round-1 code restored, all four placements failed on the JVM. This replaces my round-1 \"BOM inside a keyword\" case, which accepted any refusal and wasn't host-independent.\n\n## Commands and outcomes\n- `clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-head-test -n dao.space.store.fs-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`: 29 tests, 477 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- **Node:** `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge '{:ns-regexp \"yin\\\\.repl\\\\.dht-head-test\"}'`, using the `--config-merge`/`:ns-regexp` mechanism `build-n-test.md` documents for `test:slow:cljs`. The output shows \"Testing yin.repl.dht-head-test\": 18 tests, 190 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- **Dart:** `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yin.repl.dht-head-test`: all 18 tests passed, with no new warnings in `dht_head_test.cljc`.\n- `bb test:clj`: 3394 tests, 233191 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\nThe logs are in the worktree's `target/` as `h3f-r2-*.log`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
